SAFETY-NETTING ADVICE

The itching is caused by bile salts accumulating in the skin, not an allergy. If extreme abdominal pain or high fevers develop, medical care must be sought immediately as this indicates a potential severe blockage or infection.

PATIENT EDUCATION

Treatment Explanation: The immune system is mistakenly attacking the microscopic bile drainage tubes inside the liver. Because the tubes are damaged, bile salts are leaking back into the bloodstream and depositing in the skin, acting as a severe chemical irritant that causes the unbearable itch. Standard allergy tablets will not work because this is not a histamine reaction. The prescribed powder acts like a sponge in the bowel, actively soaking up the bile salts so the body can excrete them.
Actionable Steps: Keep fingernails cut extremely short and wear soft cotton gloves at night. This physically prevents the deep, severe excoriations and secondary bacterial skin infections caused by uncontrolled scratching during sleep.

